-- system-package tree, and Oracle label-security package tree is included exactly once.
-- Documented signatures, overloads, parameter tables, defaults, options, constants,
-- return values, exceptions, restrictions, and notes are preserved as SQL comments.
-- Official example code is cleaned of client prompts/result grids and also commented.
-- ANYDATA and XMLType are included because they are documented in the official Oracle
-- system-package tree, although they are types rather than DBMS_* packages.
--
-- IMPORTANT SAFETY BOUNDARY
-- Do not execute this entire file. Administrative, resource, scheduler, statistics,
-- workload, security, file/network, DDL, and cryptographic operations can change state,
-- affect performance, or access external systems. Test individual examples only in an
-- isolated tenant/schema with the required privileges and operational approval.
--
-- VALIDATION BOUNDARY
-- This is a source-coverage and static artifact check, not a live-server execution test.
-- Check your exact 4.4.2 BP, tenant mode, edition, deployment options, and privileges.
