--   ADD_TRUSTED_CERTIFICATE
--   The ADD_TRUSTED_CERTIFICATE procedure adds a CA root certificate so that components such as an OBServer cluster or OMS can securely authenticate and connect to the cluster through RPC using digital certificates issued by the certificate.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   PROCEDURE ADD_TRUSTED_CERTIFICATE(
--     common_name VARCHAR(256),
--     description VARCHAR(256),
--     content     LONGTEXT);
