--   UPDATE_TRUSTED_CERTIFICATE
--   The UPDATE_TRUSTED_CERTIFICATE procedure is used to update the CA root certificate information trusted by the OBServer cluster.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   PROCEDURE UPDATE_TRUSTED_CERTIFICATE(
--     common_name VARCHAR(256),
--     description VARCHAR(256),
--     content     LONGTEXT);
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   common_name | The unique identifier of the certificate, used to distinguish different certificates.
--   description | Describes the purpose of the certificate or the associated cluster information.
--   content | The detailed information of the certificate.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   CALL DBMS_TRUSTED_CERTIFICATE_MANAGER.UPDATE_TRUSTED_CERTIFICATE
