-- Package/type: DBMS_WORKLOAD_REPOSITORY
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/17900.dbms-workload-repository-mysql/200.ash-report-mysql.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/17900.dbms-workload-repository-mysql/200.ash-report-mysql.md
--   ASH_REPORT
--   The ASH_REPORT procedure displays the ASH report in text format.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   PROCEDURE ASH_REPORT(BTIME         IN DATE,
--                          ETIME         IN DATE,
--                          SQL_ID        IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT NULL,
--                          TRACE_ID      IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT NULL,
--                          WAIT_CLASS    IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT NULL,
--                          REPORT_TYPE   IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT 'text',
--                          SVR_IP        IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT NULL,
--                          SVR_PORT      IN NUMBER    DEFAULT NULL,
--                          TENANT_ID     INT          DEFAULT NULL
--                        );
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   BTIME | The start time of the sampling period.
--   ETIME | The end time of the sampling period.
--   SQL_ID | The SQL_ID of the SQL statement to be sampled. If this parameter is not specified or set to NULL, no restriction is applied to SQL_ID.
--   TRACE_ID | The TRACE_ID of the SQL statement to be sampled. If this parameter is not specified or set to NULL, no restriction is applied to TRACE_ID.
--   WAIT_CLASS | The event type to be sampled. Valid values are the same as those of the WAIT_CLASS column in the GV$ACTIVE_SESSION_HISTORY view. If this parameter is not specified or set to NULL, no restriction is applied to the wait type.
--   REPORT_TYPE | The report type. Valid values are HTML and TEXT. If this parameter is not specified, the default value TEXT is used.
--   SVR_IP | The IP address of the node to generate the ASH report. If this parameter is not specified or set to NULL, no restriction is applied to the IP address.
--   SVR_PORT | The port of the node to generate the ASH report. If this parameter is not specified or set to NULL, no restriction is applied to the port.
--   TENANT_ID | The ID of the tenant to generate the ASH report. If this parameter is not specified or set to NULL, no restriction is applied to the tenant ID.
--   Considerations
--   To obtain ASH-related information, query the GV$ACTIVE_SESSION_HISTORY view.
--   Examples
--   Call the ASH_REPORT procedure and specify the start and end times for the diagnostic period. After the procedure is executed, the ASH report is displayed on the interface.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   CALL DBMS_WORKLOAD_REPOSITORY.ASH_REPORT( '2023-12-25 10:15:00',  '2023-12-25 10:19:02' );
--   The following is an example of the output:
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   REPORT:
--   # ASH Report
--
--   ----
--              Sample Begin: 2023-12-25 10:15:00
--                Sample End: 2023-12-25 10:19:02
--                ----------
--       Analysis Begin Time: 2023-12-25 10:15:00
--         Analysis End Time: 2023-12-25 10:19:02
--              Elapsed Time: 242
--             Num of Sample: 611
--             Num of Events: 611
--   Average Active Sessions: 2.52
--   ----
--
--   ## Top User Events:
--   Execute the following command to display the report in HTML format.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   CALL DBMS_WORKLOAD_REPOSITORY.ASH_REPORT('2024-04-22 19:26:47', '2024-06-22 19:27:07', null, null, null, 'HTML', '172.30.xxx.xxx', 28xx)\G
