-- [M12-0001] Overview
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/100.dbms-xplan-overview-mysql.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/100.dbms-xplan-overview-mysql.md
--   Overview
--   The DBMS_XPLAN package provides features for the management of logical plans, such as optimizing and tracing logical plans.
--   Privileges
--   To use the package, you must have the privileges to execute PL SQL statements.
--   Subprograms
--   The following table describes the DBMS_XPLAN subprograms supported by the current OceanBase Database version.
--   Subprogram | Description
--   DISPLAY_ACTIVE_SESSION_PLAN | Displays the details of the active execution plan in the specified session.
--   DISPLAY_CURSOR | Displays the details of an executed query plan.
--   DISPLAY | Displays the execution plan generated for an SQL statement after the statement is explained by EXPLAIN.
--   DISABLE_OPT_TRACE | Disables end-to-end tracing for the optimizer of the current session.
--   DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE | Displays a baseline plan in SQL Plan Management (SPM).
--   ENABLE_OPT_TRACE | Enables end-to-end tracing for the optimizer of the current session.
--   SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER | Sets end-to-end tracing parameters for the optimizer of the current session.

-- [M12-0002] DISPLAY_ACTIVE_SESSION_PLAN
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/200.display-active-session-plan-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/200.display-active-session-plan-of-mysql-mode.md
--   DISPLAY_ACTIVE_SESSION_PLAN
--   The DISPLAY_ACTIVE_SESSION_PLAN function displays the real-time plan details of the specified session.
--   Function definition
-- Documented declaration or code block (commented); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY_ACTIVE_SESSION_PLAN(
--              session_id   INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
--              format       VARCHAR2  DEFAULT  'TYPICAL',
--              svr_ip       VARCHAR2  DEFAULT  NULL,      -- default value: server connected by client
--              svr_port     INTEGER DEFAULT 0           -- default value: server connected by client
--              )
--   return DISPLAY_ACTIVE_SESSION_PLAN;
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   session_id | The session ID of the user. This is not the proxy session ID, but the server session ID.
--   format | The plan format. Valid values: • 'BASIC': displays basic information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator comment, and expression. ; 'TYPICAL': displays basic information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator comment, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, and expression. If the plan has been executed, it also displays the actual feedback of the plan, such as the actual number of rows and cost. ; 'ALL': displays rich plan information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator comment, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, and expression. It also displays the effective hint, query block name trace, outline, base table optimization, constant parameterization, constraint, and plan note. ; 'ADVANCED': displays rich plan information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator comment, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, and expression. It also displays the effective hint, query block name trace, outline, base table optimization, constant parameterization, constraint, and plan note. In addition, it displays the tree structure of complex plans.
--   svr_ip | The IP address of the node where the plan is located. The default value is the IP address of the node to which the session is connected.
--   svr_port | The port number of the node where the plan is located. The default value is the port number of the node to which the session is connected.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   /* Execute a slow SQL statement. */
--   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM TABLE(GENERATOR(100000)) A, TABLE(GENERATOR(10000))B;
--   /* Connect to another session and query the session ID of the SQL statement that is being executed by using the SHOW PROCESSLIST command. */
--   SHOW PROCESSLIST;
--   /* Display session plan details */
--   SELECT DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY_ACTIVE_SESSION_PLAN(3221668463);

-- [M12-0003] DISPLAY_CURSOR
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/300.display-cursor-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/300.display-cursor-of-mysql-mode.md
--   DISPLAY_CURSOR
--   The DISPLAY_CURSOR function is used to display the details of the executed query plan.
--   Limitations
--   For V4.3.5, this feature is supported starting from V4.3.5 BP2.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY_CURSOR(plan_id      DECIMAL          DEFAULT    0,         -- default value: last plan
--                             format       VARCHAR(32)      DEFAULT    'TYPICAL',
--                             svr_ip       VARCHAR(64)      DEFAULT    null,   -- default value: server connected by client
--                             svr_port     DECIMAL          DEFAULT    0,     -- default value: server connected by client
--                             tenant_id    DECIMAL          DEFAULT    0,     -- default value: current tenant
--                             sql_handle   VARCHAR(32)      DEFAULT    NULL,
--                             plan_name    VARCHAR(32)      DEFAULT    NULL
--                           )
--   RETURN DBMS_XPLAN_TYPE_TABLE;
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   plan_id | The ID of the execution plan. If not specified, the plan from the last execution is used.
--   format | Specifies the plan format information. The optional parameters are as follows:• 'BASIC': displays a small amount of information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, and expression information.; 'TYPICAL': displays basic information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, and expression information. If the plan has been executed, it also displays the actual feedback information from the first execution, such as actual rows and cost.; 'ALL': displays rich plan information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, expression information, effective hints, query block name trace information, outline information, base table optimization information, constant parameterization information, constraint information, and plan notes.; 'ADVANCED': displays rich plan information, which is the same as the 'ALL' parameter. Additionally, it displays tree structure information for complex plans.
--   svr_ip | The IP address of the node where the plan is located. The default value is the IP address of the node to which the session is connected.
--   svr_port | The port number of the node where the plan is located. The default value is the port number of the node to which the session is connected.
--   tenant_id | The tenant ID to which the plan belongs. The default value is the tenant to which the session is currently connected.
--   sql_handle | The handle (Handle) used to identify the SQL statement for the execution plan. When querying a specific execution plan for an SQL statement, if there are multiple similar SQL statements, you can use sql_handle to precisely specify the target statement.
--   plan_name | The name of the execution plan.
--   Examples
--   MySQL-compatible tenants do not have the Function Table feature, so the DISPLAY_CURSOR function can be directly used in SELECT statements to output plan information.
--   1. Create a table.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   CREATE TABLE t1(c1 INT);
--   2. Execute a query.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   SELECT * FROM t1;
--   3. Use the DBMS_XPLAN package to view historical plans.
--   • Query without specifying parameters.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   SELECT DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY_CURSOR() ;
--   The query result is as follows:
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--        |0 |TABLE FULL SCAN|t1  |1       |4           |0        |0            |0          |155         |
--        -------------------------------------
--          0 - output([t1.c1]), filter(nil), rowset=16
--              access([t1.c1]), partitions(p0)
--              is_index_back=false, is_global_index=false,
--              range_key([t1.__pk_increment]), range(MIN ; MAX)always true
--
--        |
--   • Query by specifying parameters.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   SELECT DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY_CURSOR(67475, 'typical', '11.xxx.xxx.xxx', 32903, 1, 'AE3BAF04FD13DF0DC5B4B9C6EFA9C8CA', '3290318591324336132') FROM DUAL;
--   The query result is as follows:
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--        |0 |DISTRIBUTED INSERT|    |1       |13          |0        |0            |0          |488         |
--        |1 |└─EXPRESSION      |    |1       |1           |1        |0            |0          |20          |
--        -------------------------------------
--         0 - output(nil), filter(nil)
--             columns([{test_sqlstat: ({test_sqlstat: (test_sqlstat.a, test_sqlstat.b)})}]),
--             column_values([column_conv(INT,PS:(11,0),NOT NULL,__values.a)], [column_conv(INT,PS:(11,0),NULL,__values.b)])
--         1 - output([__values.a], [__values.b]), filter(nil)
--             values({3, 3})
--
--        |

-- [M12-0004] DISPLAY
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/400.display-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/400.display-of-mysql-mode.md
--   DISPLAY
--   The DISPLAY function is used to query and format historical EXPLAIN plans.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   TYPE DBMS_XPLAN_TYPE_TABLE IS TABLE OF VARCHAR2(4000);
--
--   DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY(format VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'TYPICAL',
--                     statement_id VARCHAR2 DEFAULT null,
--                     table_name   VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'PLAN_TABLE',
--                     filter_preds VARCHAR2 DEFAULT null)
--   RETURN DBMS_XPLAN_TYPE_TABLE;
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   format | Specifies the plan format information. The optional values are as follows:• 'BASIC': displays a small amount of information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, and expression information.; 'TYPICAL': displays basic information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, and expression information. If the plan has been executed, it also displays the actual feedback information from the first execution, such as actual rows and cost.; 'ALL': displays rich plan information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, expression information, effective hints, query block name trace information, outline information, base table optimization information, constant parameterization information, constraint information, and plan note.; 'ADVANCED': displays rich plan information, which is the same as the 'ALL' parameter. In addition, it displays tree structure information for complex plans.
--   statement_id | The marker information for the EXPLAIN query. You can set the marker information for the query by using the EXPLAIN SET STATEMENT_ID='XXX' command.
--   table_name | The target table for saving the EXPLAIN plan. The default value is PLAN_TABLE.
--   filter_preds | Additional PLAN_TABLE filter conditions for filtering specific operators or plans.
--   Examples
--   If you use the DISPLAY function in a SELECT statement, you can view execution plans for the statement in MySQL-compatible tenants. This function is not available in TIDB instances.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   -- Connect to the database and create a table.
--   CREATE TABLE t1 (c1 INT);
--   CREATE TABLE plan_table (
--       statement_id VARCHAR(30),
--       plan_id INT,
--       gmt_create TIMESTAMP,
--       remarks VARCHAR(4000),
--       operator VARCHAR(255),
--       options VARCHAR(255),
--       object_node VARCHAR(40),
--       object_owner VARCHAR(128),
--       object_name VARCHAR(128),
--       object_alias VARCHAR(261),
--       object_instance INT,
--       object_type VARCHAR(30),
--       optimizer VARCHAR(4000),
--       search_columns INT,
--       id INT,
--       parent_id INT,
--       depth INT,
--       position INT,
--       is_last_child INT,
--       cost INT,
--       cardinality INT,
--       bytes INT,
--       rowset INT,
--       other_tag VARCHAR(4000),
--       partition_start VARCHAR(4000),
--       partition_stop VARCHAR(4000),
--       partition_id INT,
--       other VARCHAR(4000),
--       distribution VARCHAR(64),
--       cpu_cost INT,
--       io_cost INT,
--       temp_space INT,
--       access_predicates VARCHAR(4000),
--       filter_predicates VARCHAR(4000),
--       startup_predicates VARCHAR(4000),
--       projection VARCHAR(4000),
--       special_predicates VARCHAR(4000),
--       time INT,
--       qblock_name VARCHAR(128),
--       other_xml VARCHAR(4000)
--   );
--
--   -- Use EXPLAIN to view the query plan.
--   EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM t1;
--   -- View the historical plans by using the DBMS_XPLAN package.
--   SELECT dbms_xplan.display() FROM dual;
--   -----------------------------------------------
--   |0 |TABLE FULL SCAN|t1  |1       |4           |
--   -------------------------------------
--     0 - output([t1.c1]), filter(nil), rowset=16
--         access([t1.c1]), partitions(p0)
--         is_index_back=false, is_global_index=false,
--         range_key([t1.__pk_increment]), range(MIN ; MAX)always true
--
--    |

