-- [M12-0006] DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/600.display-sql-plan-baseline-of-mysql-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/600.display-sql-plan-baseline-of-mysql-mode.md
--   DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE
--   The DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE function is used to view the baseline plans in the SPM.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE(
--              sql_handle   VARCHAR2  DEFAULT  NULL,
--              plan_name    VARCHAR2  DEFAULT  NULL,
--              format       VARCHAR2  DEFAULT  'TYPICAL',
--              svr_ip       VARCHAR2 DEFAULT null,   -- default value: server connected by client
--              svr_port     INTEGER DEFAULT 0,     -- default value: server connected by client
--              tenant_id    INTEGER DEFAULT 0     -- default value: current tenant)
--   RETURN DBMS_XPLAN_TYPE_TABLE;
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   sql_handle | The SQL handle of the baseline plan, which can be obtained from the SPM views.
--   plan_name | The name of the baseline plan.
--   format | The plan format. Valid values: • 'BASIC': displays basic information such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, and expression information. ; 'TYPICAL': displays basic information such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, and expression information. If the plan has been executed, it also displays the actual feedback information of the plan's first execution, such as actual rows and cost. ; 'ALL': displays rich plan information such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, and expression information, as well as effective hints, query block name trace information, outline information, base table optimization information, constant parameterization information, constraint information, and plan notes. ; 'ADVANCED': displays rich plan information, which is the same as the 'ALL' parameter. In addition, it displays tree structure information for complex plans.
--   svr_ip | The IP address of the node where the plan is located. The default value is the IP address of the node to which the session is connected.
--   svr_port | The port number of the node where the plan is located. The default value is the port number of the node to which the session is connected.
--   tenant_id | The tenant ID to which the plan belongs. The default value is the tenant ID to which the session is connected.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   /* Enable SPM for the current session. */
--   SET SESSION optimizer_use_sql_plan_baselines = 'ON';
--   SET SESSION optimizer_capture_sql_plan_baselines = 'ON';
--
--   /* Create a baseline plan. */
--   CREATE TABLE t1(c1 INT);
--   SELECT * FROM t1 WHERE c1 > 1;
--
--   /* Query the ID of the baseline plan. */
--   SELECT sql_handle,plan_name FROM oceanbase.DBA_SQL_PLAN_BASELINES;
--   /* View the baseline plan */
--   SELECT DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE('49D6048C041AA8C7E70E2D114250AB99','11986391583431335905','all');

-- [M12-0007] ENABLE_OPT_TRACE
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/800.enable-opt-trace-mysql.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/800.enable-opt-trace-mysql.md
--   ENABLE_OPT_TRACE
--   The ENABLE_OPT_TRACE procedure enables full optimizer tracing. After it is enabled, the tracing process will be performed for each plan generation in the current session, including the plan generation process of SQL statements within PL/SQL blocks. A tracing file will be generated in the execution node log directory of the SQL statement.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DEFAULT_INENTIFIER  constant VARCHAR2(20) := '';
--   DEFAULT_LEVEL       constant INT := 1;
--
--   DBMS_XPLAN.ENABLE_OPT_TRACE(
--       sql_id          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT '',
--       identifier      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT DEFAULT_INENTIFIER,
--       level           IN INT DEFAULT DEFAULT_LEVEL
--   );
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   sql_id | Specifies the SQL statement to be traced. For example, if you want to trace only specific SQL statements within PL/SQL functions during the current test, you can set the sql_id parameter. Once sql_id is set, only the specified SQL statements will be traced; otherwise, all SQL statements will be traced.
--   identifier | Specifies the suffix of the trace file, making it easier for users to locate their trace files.
--   level | Specifies the tracing level: • 0: Default behavior.; 1: Additional information about memory and time usage for each module.; 2: Additional information about rewritten query blocks, regardless of whether they are rewritten. ; Note: level is a database keyword. In an Oracle-compatible tenant, it must be enclosed in double quotation marks (""). In a MySQL-compatible tenant, it must be enclosed in backticks ().
--   Examples
--   Enable optimizer tracing for the current session.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   /* Connect to the database and enable optimizer tracing for the current session */
--   CALL DBMS_XPLAN.ENABLE_OPT_TRACE();
--
--   /* Set the trace log level and file suffix */
--   CALL DBMS_XPLAN.SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER(identifier=>'trace_test', `level`=>3);
--
--   /* Execute a query */
--   SELECT * FROM t1;
--   Empty set
--
--   /* View the trace log with the suffix "trace_test" in the log directory of the OBServer node */
--   vi /data/1/observer/log/optimizer_trace_BkkGn1_trace_test.trac
--
--   /* Disable optimizer tracing for the current session */
--   CALL DBMS_XPLAN.DISABLE_OPT_TRACE();;

-- [M12-0008] SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER
-- Mode: MySQL
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/1000.set-opt-trace-parameter-mysql.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/200.pl-mysql/1000.pl-system-package-mysql/20700.dbms-xplan-mysql/1000.set-opt-trace-parameter-mysql.md
--   SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER
--   The SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER procedure sets end-to-end tracing parameters for the optimizer of the current session.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XPLAN.SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER(
--       sql_id          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT '',
--       identifier      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT DEFAULT_INENTIFIER,
--       level           IN INT DEFAULT DEFAULT_LEVEL
--   );
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   sql_id | The ID of the SQL statement to be traced. For example, if you want to run a PL program in a test and trace only a specific SQL statement in a PL function, you can specify sql_id to mark that SQL statement. If you do not specify a sql_id, all SQL statements are traced.
--   identifier | The suffix of the trace file, which helps you easily find the trace file.
--   level | The level of tracing. Valid values: • 0: Perform default actions. ; 1: Print the memory usage and running duration of each module apart from performing level-0 tracing actions. ; 2: Print the SQL statement corresponding to each rewrite query block, regardless of whether the SQL statement is rewritten or not, apart from performing level-0 and level-1 tracing actions. ; Note: level is a database keyword and therefore must be enclosed by double quotation marks (" ") in an Oracle-compatible tenant and by grave accents (\ \) in a MySQL-compatible tenant.
--   Examples
--   Specify level and the log file suffix for trace logs.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   CALL DBMS_XPLAN.SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER(identifier=>'trace_test', `level`=>2);

