-- [O01-0001] Overview
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/1900.dbms-application-info-oracle/100.dbms-application-info-overview-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/1900.dbms-application-info-oracle/100.dbms-application-info-overview-oracle.md
--   Overview
--   The DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO package registers application names with the database for auditing or performance tracking purposes.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Privileges
--   No special privileges are required for the use of the DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO package. When the application registers with the database, its name and operation are recorded in the GV$OB_PROCESSLIST view.
--   Subprograms
--   The following table describes the DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO subprograms supported by the current OceanBase Database version.
--   Subprogram | Description
--   READ_CLIENT_INFO | Reads the value of the client_info field of the current session.
--   READ_MODULE | Reads the values of the module and action fields of the current session.
--   SET_ACTION | Sets the name of the current operation in the current module.
--   SET_CLIENT_INFO | Sets additional information for the client application.
--   SET_MODULE | Renames the running module as a new module.

-- [O01-0002] READ_CLIENT_INFO
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/1900.dbms-application-info-oracle/200.read-client-info-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/1900.dbms-application-info-oracle/200.read-client-info-oracle.md
--   READ_CLIENT_INFO
--   The READ_CLIENT_INFO procedure reads the value of the client_info field of the current session.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO.READ_CLIENT_INFO (
--      client_info OUT VARCHAR2);
--   Parameters
--   The client_info parameter provides the latest client information for the SET_CLIENT_INFO procedure.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   DECLARE
--       myclient VARCHAR2(50);
--       mymodule VARCHAR2(50);
--       myaction VARCHAR2(50);
--
--      BEGIN
--         DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO.SET_CLIENT_INFO('OBClient');
--         DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO.READ_CLIENT_INFO(myclient);
--         DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE ('client='||myclient);
--         DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO.SET_MODULE('OBmodule','inserting');
--         DBMS_APPLICATION_INFO.READ_MODULE(mymodule,myaction);
--         DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('mod_name='||mymodule);
--         DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('act_name='||myaction);
--      END;
--
--   client=OBClient
--   mod_name=OBmodule
--   act_name=inserting

