-- [O05-0014] INITIALIZE
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_DEBUG
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/5300.dbms-debug-oracle/1400.initialize-debug-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/5300.dbms-debug-oracle/1400.initialize-debug-oracle.md
--   INITIALIZE
--   The INITIALIZE function initializes the target session for debugging.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_DEBUG.INITIALIZE (
--      debug_session_id  IN VARCHAR2       := NULL,
--      diagnostics       IN BINARY_INTEGER := 0)
--     RETURN VARCHAR2;
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   debug_session_id | The ID of the target session. A unique ID is generated if the value of this parameter is NULL.
--   diagnostics | Specifies whether to dump the output of diagnostics to the trace file. Valid values: • 0: No diagnostics. This is the default value. ; 1: Print diagnostics.
--   Note
--   Only the default value is supported. An error is reported if a non-default value is passed.
--   Return values
--   The ID of the newly registered debugging session.
--   Considerations
--   • The CREATE ANY PROCEDURE privilege does not affect the visibility of routines through the debugger. A DEBUG privilege with a corresponding DEBUG ANY PROCEDURE variant is introduced for each object. These are required if you want to see routines of users other than the session's login user.
--   • The checks that the debugger makes after this call to look for the DEBUG privilege on individual procedures are performed in the context of the session's login user, the roles that were enabled on the session level when the call was made, even if those roles were unavailable within a definer's rights environment of the call, and the debug role.

