--   END;
--   /

-- [O21-0009] IS_ROLE_ENABLED
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_SESSION
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/14500.dbms-session-oracle/1800.is-role-enabled-of-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/14500.dbms-session-oracle/1800.is-role-enabled-of-oracle.md
--   IS_ROLE_ENABLED
--   IS_ROLE_ENABLED determines whether the specified role is enabled in the current session.
--   Note
--   This subprogram was introduced in V4.4.1.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_SESSION.IS_ROLE_ENABLED (
--      rolename    VARCHAR2)
--     RETURN BOOLEAN;
--   Parameters
--   rolename specifies the name of the role. It returns TRUE if the role is enabled, and FALSE if the role is not enabled.
--   Example
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   BEGIN
--     IF DBMS_SESSION.IS_ROLE_ENABLED('DBA') THEN
--       DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Role DBA is enabled');
--     ELSE
--       DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Role DBA is not enabled');
--     END IF;
--   END;
--   /

