-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/17900.dbms-utility-oracle/1000.get-hash-value-oracle.md
--   GET_HASH_VALUE
--   The GET_HASH_VALUE function calculates the hash value of a specified string.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_UTILITY.GET_HASH_VALUE (
--       name        VARCHAR2,
--       base          NUMBER,
--       hash_size   NUMBER)
--     RETURN NUMBER;
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   name | The string to be hashed.
--   base | The base value at which hash values start to be generated.
--   hash_size | The required size of the hash table.
--   Return values
--   A hash value based on the input string is returned. For example, to obtain the hash value of a string with a hash value between 1000 and 3047, you can use 1000 as the base value and 2048 as the hash_size value. We recommend that you set hash_size to a power of 2.

-- [O25-0010] GET_PARAMETER_VALUE
