--   Overview
--   The DBMS_WORKLOAD_REPOSITORY package manages the Automatic Workload Repository (AWR).
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Privileges
--   To call the subprograms of the DBMS_WORKLOAD_REPOSITORY package, you must have the EXECUTE privilege.
--   Subprograms
--   The following table describes the DBMS_WORKLOAD_REPOSITORY subprograms supported by the current OceanBase Database version.
--   Subprogram | Description
--   ASH_REPORT | Displays the Active Session History (ASH) report in text.

-- [O26-0002] ASH_REPORT
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_WORKLOAD_REPOSITORY
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/18400.dbms-workload-repository-oracle/200.ash-report-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/18400.dbms-workload-repository-oracle/200.ash-report-oracle.md
--   ASH_REPORT
--   The ASH_REPORT procedure displays the ASH report in text format.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   PROCEDURE ASH_REPORT(BTIME         IN DATE,
--                          ETIME         IN DATE,
--                          SQL_ID        IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT NULL,
--                          TRACE_ID      IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT NULL,
--                          WAIT_CLASS    IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT NULL,
--                          REPORT_TYPE   IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT 'text',
--                          SVR_IP        IN VARCHAR2  DEFAULT NULL,
--                          SVR_PORT      IN NUMBER    DEFAULT NULL,
--                          TENANT_ID     IN NUMBER    DEFAULT NULL
--                        );
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   BTIME | The start time of the sampling period.
--   ETIME | The end time of the sampling period.
--   SQL_ID | The SQL_ID of the SQL statement to be sampled. If this parameter is not specified or is set to NULL, no restriction is imposed on SQL_ID.
--   TRACE_ID | The TRACE_ID of the SQL statement to be sampled. If this parameter is not specified or is set to NULL, no restriction is imposed on TRACE_ID.
--   WAIT_CLASS | The event type to be sampled. WAIT_CLASS can be set to any value in the GV$ACTIVE_SESSION_HISTORY.WAIT_CLASS column. If this parameter is not specified or is set to NULL, no restriction is imposed on the wait type.
--   REPORT_TYPE | The report type. Only the TEXT type is supported. This parameter is optional.
--   REPORT_TYPE | The report type. The HTML and TEXT types are supported. If this parameter is not specified, the default value is TEXT.
--   SVR_IP | The IP address of the node that generates the ASH report. If this parameter is not specified or is set to NULL, no restriction is imposed on the IP address.
--   SVR_PORT | The port number of the node that generates the ASH report. If this parameter is not specified or is set to NULL, no restriction is imposed on the port number.
--   TENANT_ID | The tenant ID of the tenant that generates the ASH report. If this parameter is not specified or is set to NULL, no restriction is imposed on the TENANT_ID.
--   Considerations
--   To obtain ASH information, query the oceanbase.GV$ACTIVE_SESSION_HISTORY view.
--   Examples
--   Enable server output.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   SET SERVEROUTPUT ON;
--   Call the ASH_REPORT procedure and specify the start and end times for the diagnostic period. After the procedure is executed, the ASH report is displayed on the interface.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
