-- [O28-0015] NEWDOMDOCUMENT
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_XMLDOM
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19500.dbms-xmldom-oracle/1500.newdomdocument-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19500.dbms-xmldom-oracle/1500.newdomdocument-oracle.md
--   NEWDOMDOCUMENT
--   The NEWDOMDOCUMENT function creates a new, empty DOM document object. You can then set the document version and character set, create a root element, append child nodes, and finally serialize or convert it to an XMLType.
--   Applicability
--   This content applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Note
