-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19500.dbms-xmldom-oracle/2300.getdocumentelement-oracle.md
--   GETDOCUMENTELEMENT
--   The GETDOCUMENTELEMENT function returns the root element node of a DOM document. This interface serves as a common entry point for traversing the element tree, reading attributes, and manipulating child nodes from a document object.
--   Applicability
--   This content applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Note
--   For V4.4.2, this subprogram is available starting with OceanBase Database V4.4.2 BP3.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.getDocumentElement (
--      doc IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMDOCUMENT);
--   Parameters
--   Parameters | Explanation
--   doc | TargetDBMS_XMLDOM.DOMDOCUMENTHandle.
--   Return value
--   The root element handle of DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMELEMENT.
--   Usage instructions
--   If the document has no root element, an empty handle is returned. You can use ISNULL to check whether the return value is null.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   DECLARE
--     doc  DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMDOCUMENT;
--     elem DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMELEMENT;
--   BEGIN
--     doc := DBMS_XMLDOM.newDOMDocument;
--     elem := DBMS_XMLDOM.getDocumentElement(doc);
--     DBMS_XMLDOM.freeDocument(doc);
--   END;
--   /

-- [O28-0024] GETNODENAME
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_XMLDOM
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19500.dbms-xmldom-oracle/2400.getnodename-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19500.dbms-xmldom-oracle/2400.getnodename-oracle.md
--   GETNODENAME
--   The GETNODENAME function is used to obtain the node name of a specified DOM node. Element nodes return the element name, attribute nodes return the attribute name, and text nodes return the corresponding node name according to Oracle DOM semantics.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Note
--   For V4.4.2, this subprogram is available starting with OceanBase Database V4.4.2 BP3.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.getNodeName (
--      n IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMNODE);
--   Parameters
--   Parameters | Explanation
--   n | To query theDBMS_XMLDOM.DOMNODEHandle.
--   Return value
--   Node name, of type VARCHAR2.
--   Usage instructions
--   For elements with a namespace prefix, the return value can include the prefix. If only the local name is needed, use GETLOCALNAME.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   DECLARE
--     n         DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMNODE;
--     node_name VARCHAR2(32767);
--   BEGIN
--     node_name := DBMS_XMLDOM.getNodeName(n);
--   END;
--   /

-- [O28-0025] GETLOCALNAME
