-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19500.dbms-xmldom-oracle/2800.isnull-oracle.md
--   ISNULL
--   The ISNULL function is used to determine whether a DOM handle is null. It is commonly used to check for null values in return results from interfaces such as GETFIRSTCHILD, GETDOCUMENTELEMENT, and MAKENODE.
--   Applicability
--   This content applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Note
--   For V4.4.2, this subprogram is available starting with OceanBase Database V4.4.2 BP3.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.isNull (
--      n IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMNODE);
--
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.isNull (
--      doc IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMDOCUMENT);
--
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.isNull (
--      elem IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMELEMENT);
--
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.isNull (
--      text IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMTEXT);
--
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.isNull (
--      attr IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMATTR);
--
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.isNull (
--      character_data IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMCHARACTERDATA);
--   Parameters
--   Parameters | Explanation
--   n / doc / elem / text / attr / character_data | The DOM handle to be checked.
--   Return value
--   If the handle is null, TRUE is returned; otherwise, FALSE is returned.
--   Usage instructions
--   The different overloads accept various DOM handles; it is recommended to call this function first to check for null values before proceeding to access the node.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   DECLARE
--     n       DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMNODE;
--     is_null BOOLEAN;
--   BEGIN
--     is_null := DBMS_XMLDOM.isNull(n);
--   END;
--   /

