-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19500.dbms-xmldom-oracle/3200.writetobuffer-oracle.md
--   WRITETOBUFFER
--   The WRITETOBUFFER procedure serializes a DOM document or DOM node and writes it to a VARCHAR2 buffer, facilitating further processing or returning the XML text in PL/SQL.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Note
--   For V4.4.2, this subprogram is available starting with OceanBase Database V4.4.2 BP3.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.writeToBuffer (
--      doc    IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMDOCUMENT,
--      buffer IN OUT VARCHAR2);
--
--   DBMS_XMLDOM.writeToBuffer (
--      n      IN DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMNODE,
--      buffer IN OUT VARCHAR2);
--   Parameters
--   Parameters | Explanation
--   doc / n | To be serializedDOMDOCUMENTorDOMNODEHandle.
--   buffer | Used to receive the serialized result.VARCHAR2Buffer (IN OUT).
--   Return value
--   No return value; the result is written to buffer.
--   Usage instructions
--   When the XML content may exceed the length limit of VARCHAR2, use WRITETOCLOB instead.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   DECLARE
--     doc    DBMS_XMLDOM.DOMDOCUMENT;
--     buffer VARCHAR2(32767);
--   BEGIN
--     doc := DBMS_XMLDOM.newDOMDocument;
--     DBMS_XMLDOM.writeToBuffer(doc, buffer);
--     DBMS_XMLDOM.freeDocument(doc);
--   END;
--   /

-- [O28-0033] WRITETOCLOB
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_XMLDOM
