-- [O29-0001] Overview
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_XMLGEN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19700.dbms-xmlgen-oracle/100.dbms-xmlgen-system-package-overview-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19700.dbms-xmlgen-oracle/100.dbms-xmlgen-system-package-overview-oracle.md
--   Overview
--   The DBMS_XMLGEN package converts the SQL query result into the standard XML format and returns the result as a CLOB.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Privileges
--   The EXECUTE privilege on the DBMS_XMLGEN package is granted to PUBLIC. Subprograms in this package are executed with the privileges of the current user.
--   Subprograms
--   The following table describes the DBMS_XMLGEN subprograms supported by the current OceanBase Database version.
--   Subprogram | Description
--   CONVERT | Converts XML data into escaped or unescaped XML equivalents.

-- [O29-0002] CONVERT
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_XMLGEN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19700.dbms-xmlgen-oracle/200.convert-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/19700.dbms-xmlgen-oracle/200.convert-oracle.md
--   CONVERT
--   The CONVERT function converts the XML data into escaped or unescaped XML equivalents and returns CLOB or VARCHAR2 data in an encoded or decoded format.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
--   The current OceanBase Database version supports XML data in the string or CLOB form. The syntax is as follows:
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XMLGEN.CONVERT (
--      xmlData IN VARCHAR2,
--      flag    IN NUMBER := ENTITY_ENCODE)
--   RETURN VARCHAR2;
--
--   DBMS_XMLGEN.CONVERT (
--      xmlData IN CLOB,
--      flag    IN NUMBER := ENTITY_ENCODE)
--    RETURN CLOB;
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   xmlData | The XML CLOB data to be encoded or decoded.
--   flag | The encoding/decoding flag. • ENTITY_ENCODE: the flag for encoding. This is the default value. ; ENTITY_DECODE: the flag for decoding.
--   Considerations
--   If flag is set to ENTITY_ENCODE, this function escapes XML data.
--   For example, the character > is escaped into >.
--   Unescaping is the reverse transformation.

