-- [O32-0006] DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/20700.dbms-xplan-oracle/600.display-sql-plan-baseline-of-oracle-mode.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/20700.dbms-xplan-oracle/600.display-sql-plan-baseline-of-oracle-mode.md
--   DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE
--   The DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE function is used to view the baseline plans of the SQL Plan Management (SPM) feature.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE(
--              sql_handle   VARCHAR2  DEFAULT  NULL,
--              plan_name    VARCHAR2  DEFAULT  NULL,
--              format       VARCHAR2  DEFAULT  'TYPICAL',
--              svr_ip       VARCHAR2 DEFAULT null,   -- default value: server connected by client
--              svr_port     INTEGER DEFAULT 0,     -- default value: server connected by client
--              tenant_id    INTEGER DEFAULT 0     -- default value: current tenant)
--   RETURN DBMS_XPLAN_TYPE_TABLE;
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   sql_handle | The SQL handle of the baseline plan, which can be obtained from SPM-related views.
--   plan_name | The name of the baseline plan.
--   format | The plan format. Valid values: • 'BASIC': displays minimal information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, and expression information. ; 'TYPICAL': displays basic information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, and expression information. If the plan has been executed, it also displays the actual feedback information of the plan's first execution, such as actual rows and cost. ; 'ALL': displays comprehensive plan information, such as operator ID, operator name, operator remarks, optimizer-estimated output rows, optimizer-estimated execution time, and expression information, as well as the effective hint, query block name trace, outline, base table optimization, constant parameterization, constraint, and plan note. ; 'ADVANCED': displays comprehensive plan information, which is the same as the 'ALL' parameter. In addition, it displays tree structure information for complex plans.
--   svr_ip | The IP address of the node where the plan is stored. The default value is the IP address of the node to which the session is connected.
--   svr_port | The port number of the node where the plan is stored. The default value is the port number of the node to which the session is connected.
--   tenant_id | The ID of the tenant to which the plan belongs. The default value is the ID of the tenant to which the session is connected.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   /* Enable SPM for the current session. */
--   SET SESSION optimizer_use_sql_plan_baselines = 'ON';
--   SET SESSION optimizer_capture_sql_plan_baselines = 'ON';
--
--   /* Create a baseline plan. */
--   CREATE TABLE t1(c1 INT);
--   SELECT * FROM t1 WHERE c1 > 1;
--
--   /* Query the ID of the baseline plan. */
--   SELECT sql_handle,plan_name FROM oceanbase.DBA_SQL_PLAN_BASELINES;
--   /* View the baseline plan */
--   SELECT * FROM TABLE(DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY_SQL_PLAN_BASELINE('49D6048C041AA8C7E70E2D114250AB99','11986391583431335905','all'));

-- [O32-0007] ENABLE_OPT_TRACE
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/20700.dbms-xplan-oracle/800.enable-opt-trace-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/20700.dbms-xplan-oracle/800.enable-opt-trace-oracle.md
--   ENABLE_OPT_TRACE
--   The ENABLE_OPT_TRACE procedure is used to enable full-link tracing for the optimizer. Once enabled, the tracing will capture the plan generation process for every SQL statement executed in the current session, including those generated within PL/SQL blocks, and generate a trace file in the execution node log directory.
--   Applicability
--   This content applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition only provides MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DEFAULT_INENTIFIER  constant VARCHAR2(20) := '';
--   DEFAULT_LEVEL       constant INT := 1;
--
--   DBMS_XPLAN.ENABLE_OPT_TRACE(
--       sql_id          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT '',
--       identifier      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT DEFAULT_INENTIFIER,
--       level           IN INT DEFAULT DEFAULT_LEVEL
--   );
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   sql_id | Specifies the SQL statement to be traced. For example, if you want to trace only specific SQL statements within a PL/SQL block, you can set the sql_id parameter. Once set, only the specified SQL statement will be traced; otherwise, all SQL statements will be traced.
--   identifier | Specifies the suffix for the trace file, making it easier for users to locate their trace files.
--   level | Specifies the tracing level: • 0: Default behavior.; 1: Additional information about memory and time usage for each module.; 2: Additional information about rewritten query blocks, regardless of whether they were rewritten. ; Notice: level is a database keyword. In Oracle-compatible tenants, it must be enclosed in double quotation marks (" "), while in MySQL-compatible tenants, it must be enclosed in backticks ( ).
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   /* Connect to the database and enable optimizer tracing for the current session. */
--   CALL DBMS_XPLAN.ENABLE_OPT_TRACE();
--
--   /* Set the trace level and file suffix. */
--   CALL DBMS_XPLAN.SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER(identifier=>'trace_test', "level"=>3);
--
--   /* Execute a query. */
--   SELECT * FROM t1;
--   Empty set
--
--   /* View the trace file with the suffix "trace_test" in the OBServer node log directory. */
--   vi /data/1/observer/log/optimizer_trace_BkkGn1_trace_test.trac
--
--   /* Disable optimizer tracing for the current session. */
--   CALL DBMS_XPLAN.DISABLE_OPT_TRACE();;

-- [O32-0008] SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_XPLAN
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/20700.dbms-xplan-oracle/1000.set-opt-trace-parameter-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/20700.dbms-xplan-oracle/1000.set-opt-trace-parameter-oracle.md
--   SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER
--   The SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER procedure sets end-to-end tracing parameters for the optimizer of the current session.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_XPLAN.SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER(
--       sql_id          IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT '',
--       identifier      IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT DEFAULT_INENTIFIER,
--       level           IN INT DEFAULT DEFAULT_LEVEL
--   );
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   sql_id | The ID of the SQL statement to be traced. For example, if you want to run a PL program in a test and trace only a specific SQL statement in a PL function, you can specify sql_id to mark that SQL statement. If you do not specify a sql_id, all SQL statements are traced.
--   identifier | The suffix of the trace file, which helps you easily find the trace file.
--   level | The level of tracing. Valid values: • 0: Perform default actions. ; 1: Print the memory usage and running duration of each module apart from performing level-0 tracing actions. ; 2: Print the SQL statement corresponding to each rewrite query block, regardless of whether the SQL statement is rewritten or not, apart from performing level-0 and level-1 tracing actions. ; Note: level is a database keyword and therefore must be enclosed by double quotation marks (" ") in an Oracle-compatible tenant and by grave accents (\ \) in a MySQL-compatible tenant.
--   Examples
--   Specify level and the log file suffix for trace logs.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   CALL DBMS_XPLAN.SET_OPT_TRACE_PARAMETER(identifier=>'trace_test', "level"=>2);

