--   Overview
--   The DBMS_EXTERNAL_TABLE package provides a programming interface for managing and operating external tables.
--   Subprograms
--   The following table describes the DBMS_EXTERNAL_TABLE subprograms supported by the current OceanBase Database version.
--   Subprogram | Description
--   auto_refresh_external_table | Regularly refreshes the metadata of an external table.

-- [O34-0002] AUTO_REFRESH_EXTERNAL_TABLE
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: DBMS_EXTERNAL_TABLE
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/21000.dbms-external-table-oracle/200.auto-refresh-external-table-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/21000.dbms-external-table-oracle/200.auto-refresh-external-table-oracle.md
--   AUTO_REFRESH_EXTERNAL_TABLE
--   AUTO_REFRESH_EXTERNAL_TABLE regularly refreshes the metadata of an external table.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   DBMS_EXTERNAL_TABLE.auto_refresh_external_table(interval int)
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   interval int | The interval for scheduling the refresh task, in seconds. Value range: [-1,∞]. • When the value is -1, scheduling of the refresh task is disabled. ; When the value is 0, the metadata of the external table is immediately refreshed. ; When the value is greater than 0, the metadata of the external table is refreshed based on the specified interval.
--   Examples
--   Execute the following statement to disable scheduling of the refresh task:
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   CALL DBMS_EXTERNAL_TABLE.auto_refresh_external_table(-1);

