-- [O38-0023] PUTF
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: UTL_FILE
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/26100.utl-file-oracle/1270.putf-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/26100.utl-file-oracle/1270.putf-oracle.md
--   PUTF
--   The PUTF procedure writes data to a specified file in the specified format. The procedure supports writing data to a file in the specified format, and supports writing data to a file in the specified format.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition does not support this feature.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   UTL_FILE.PUTF (
--       file   IN FILE_TYPE,
--       format IN VARCHAR2,
--       arg1   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
--       arg2   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
--       arg3   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
--       arg4   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
--       arg5   IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL
--   );
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   file | The active file handle returned by the FOPEN procedure.
--   format | The format string, which can contain the following elements: • %s: up to five placeholders that are replaced by the values of the argN parameters in sequence. • \n: a line break, which can be used multiple times in the string.
--   arg1 to arg5 | Up to five optional parameters that replace the %s placeholders in the format string. If the number of parameters is less than the number of placeholders, the un-replaced %s placeholders are retained or ignored.

