-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: UTL_RECOMP
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/26400.utl-recomp-package-oracle/500.populate-utl-recomp-skip-list-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/26400.utl-recomp-package-oracle/500.populate-utl-recomp-skip-list-oracle.md
--   POPULATE_UTL_RECOMP_SKIP_LIST
--   The POPULATE_UTL_RECOMP_SKIP_LIST procedure collects invalid objects in the current system. These invalid objects are skipped in recompilation.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   UTL_RECOMP.POPULATE_UTL_RECOMP_SKIP_LIST(
--       schema   IN   VARCHAR2    DEFAULT NULL,
--       object   IN   VARCHAR2    DEFAULT NULL,
--       flags    IN   PLS_INTEGER DEFAULT 0
--       );
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   schema | The name of the schema where the database object to be skipped in recompilation resides.
--   object | The name of the database object to be skipped in recompilation.
--   flags | The action to take if a table with the same name already exists. If a table with the same name already exists in the sys tenant, the value 512 specifies to directly use the table, and the value 1024 specifies to directly drop the table and create a new one. The default value is 0, which is optional and has no special meanings.
--   Examples
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: shell:
--   EXECUTE UTL_RECOMP.POPULATE_UTL_RECOMP_SKIP_LIST();

