-- [O46-0001] Overview
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: XMLTYPE
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/29600.xmltype-oracle/100.xmltype-overview-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/29600.xmltype-oracle/100.xmltype-overview-oracle.md
--   Overview
--   XMLType is a system-defined type for handling XML data.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only MySQL-compatible mode.
--   PL/SQL XMLType supports any SQL expression that returns an XMLType value and can use the GETCLOBVAL() and GETSTRINGVAL() methods in SQL semantics. Here are some examples:
-- Documented declaration or code block (commented); fence language: sql:
--   -- Formats the input XSL according to the xsl:stylesheet defined in it and returns the result, which is of the XMLType type.
--     MEMBER FUNCTION TRANSFORM(xsl IN XMLTYPE) RETURN XMLTYPE,
--
--     -- Convert XMLType to CLOB or VARCHAR2 Function
--     MEMBER FUNCTION GETCLOBVAL RETURN CLOB,
--     MEMBER FUNCTION GETSTRINGVAL RETURN VARCHAR2,
--
--     -- Map XMLType to PL/SQL object instances
--     MEMBER PROCEDURE TOOBJECT(object OUT NOCOPY <object_type>),
--
--     -- Converting input CLOB or VARCHAR2 data to XMLType involves performing validity checks.
--     STATIC FUNCTION CREATEXML(xmldata IN CLOB) RETURN XMLTYPE,
--     STATIC FUNCTION CREATEXML(xmldata IN VARCHAR2) RETURN XMLTYPE,
--
--     -- Construct an instance of the XMLType data type.
--     CONSTRUCTOR FUNCTION XMLTYPE(xmldata IN CLOB) RETURN SELF AS RESULT,
--     CONSTRUCTOR FUNCTION XMLTYPE(xmldata IN VARCHAR2) RETURN SELF AS RESULT
--   The following table lists the XMLType subprograms supported in the current version of OceanBase Database and their brief descriptions.
--   Subprogram | Description
--   CREATEXML | A static function for creating and returning an XMLType instance.
--   GETCLOBVAL | Returns the value of an XMLType instance in CLOB format.
--   GETSTRINGVAL | Returns the value of an XMLType instance as a string.
--   TRANSFORM | Gets an XMLType instance and an associated stylesheet (also an XMLType instance), applies the stylesheet, and returns the result as XML.
--   XMLTYPE | Constructs an instance of the XMLType data type. The constructor can accept XML data as a CLOB, VARCHAR2, or corresponding object type.
--   EXISTSNODE | Checks whether a node exists at the specified XPath path in the XML variable.
--   EXTRACT | Similar to EXISTSNODE, returns the set of nodes if they exist.
--   TOOBJECT | Maps an XMLType instance to a PL/SQL object instance (supported starting from V4.4.2 BP3).

-- [O46-0002] CREATEXML
-- Mode: Oracle
-- Package/type: XMLTYPE
-- Official source: https://github.com/oceanbase/oceanbase-doc/blob/017c8d35a015afa04ce1e1ce4b95675e3223c878/en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/29600.xmltype-oracle/200.getxml-oracle.md
-- Source file: en-US/700.reference/600.pl-reference/300.pl-oracle/1400.pl-system-package-oracle/29600.xmltype-oracle/200.getxml-oracle.md
--   CREATEXML
--   The CREATEXML static function creates and returns an XMLType instance. The CLOB parameter must contain a valid XML document in the correct format.
--   Applicability
--   This topic applies only to OceanBase Database Enterprise Edition. OceanBase Database Community Edition provides only the MySQL-compatible mode.
--   Syntax
--   The current OceanBase Database version allows you to create an XMLType instance from a string or a character large object (CLOB). The syntax is as follows:
-- Documented syntax/signature (commented; not directly executable); fence language: sql:
--   STATIC FUNCTION CREATEXML(
--          xmlData IN VARCHAR2)
--   RETURN XMLType;
--
--   STATIC FUNCTION CREATEXML(
--      xmlData IN CLOB)
--   RETURN XMLType;
--   Parameters
--   Parameter | Description
--   xmlData | The data type of the parameter. Valid values: CLOB and VARCHAR2. If the input data is a piece of text in a valid XML document, XMLType data generated based on this text is returned.
--   Examples
--   In the following example, b is a VARACHAR2 variable whose content is a piece of valid XML text. a is an XMLType variable. a:=xmltype(b) in line 5 constructs a value of the XMLType type by using b and assigns the value to the variable a.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   DECLARE
--           a XMLType;
--           b VARCHAR2(200):='<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?><note><heading>Reminder</heading></note>';
--         BEGIN
--           a:=XMLType.CREATEXML(b);
--         END;
--         /
--   If the input data is not a piece of text in a valid XML document, an error is reported.
-- Official example code (commented; setup and privileges may be required); fence language: sql:
--   DECLARE
--           a XMLType;
--           b VARCHAR2(200):='<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?><note><heading>Reminder</heading></error>';
--         BEGIN
--           a:=XMLType.CREATEXML(b);
--         END;
--         /
